.TH GCODE 1 "2026-09-30" "gcode 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gcode \- natural language to shell command generator, locally and offline
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gcode
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.B \-c
.I REQUEST
.br
.B gcode
.RB [ \-\-fix | \-\-complete
.I PARTIAL
| \-\-explain
.I COMMAND
| \-\-init ]
.br
.B gcode
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gcode
translates a natural language request into a single shell command using a local
GGUF language model and recent shell history as context. It runs entirely on the
local machine: no API key, no account, no telemetry, and no network access after
the model has been downloaded once.
.PP
Every generated command is classified into one of five risk levels
.RB ( SAFE ", " LOW ", " MEDIUM ", " HIGH ", " CRITICAL )
by a deterministic classifier that does not consult the model. Nothing is
executed without explicit confirmation unless
.B \-\-yes
is given. Commands classified
.B CRITICAL
are refused unconditionally and cannot be run by any flag or configuration
setting.
.PP
Requests may be written in English or Arabic.
.SH MODES
.TP
.B \-c ", " \-\-command " " \fIREQUEST\fR
Generate a command from a natural language request. The primary mode.
.TP
.B \-\-fix
Repair the most recent failed command from shell history, using its exit code
and error output as context.
.TP
.B \-\-complete " " \fIPARTIAL\fR
Complete a partially written command.
.TP
.B \-\-explain " " \fICOMMAND\fR
Explain an existing command: what it does, what it touches, and its risk level.
Never executes and never generates.
.TP
.B \-\-init
Install, check, or remove the shell history hook. See
.B \-\-init
under OPTIONS.
.TP
.B \-\-doctor
Print a full health report: binary, model, shell hook, permissions, resources,
and measured inference latency.
.PP
With no mode flag, gcode starts an interactive session in which each turn
inherits the context of the previous turns.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Input
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-command " " \fIREQUEST\fR
The natural language request.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Debug logging to standard error.
.SS Execution control
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Skip the confirmation prompt. Classification, the risk line, and history logging
still apply. Does not permit
.B CRITICAL
commands.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-no
Print the generated command and risk level without executing. Same as
.BR \-\-dry\-run .
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Print the command and its risk level, then exit.
.TP
.B \-\-edit
Open
.B $EDITOR
on the generated command before confirmation. The edited command is
re-classified, and a command that becomes
.B CRITICAL
is refused again.
.SS Context
.TP
.BI \-\-context " " \fIN\fR
Read the last
.I N
history entries as context. Maximum 1000. Defaults to the
.B context.history_entries
configuration value, 15 out of the box.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-history
Ignore shell history entirely.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-git
Do not include git branch and status in the prompt.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-env
Do not include operating system, shell, and working directory in the prompt.
.TP
.BI \-\-in " " \fIDIR\fR
Build context as if the working directory were
.IR DIR ,
without changing directory.
.SS Model
.TP
.BI \-\-model " " \fIPATH_OR_NAME\fR
Use a specific GGUF file or a registry model name for this invocation.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-models
List the models in the registry with sizes and checksums.
.TP
.BI \-\-download\-model " " [\fINAME\fR]
Download a model. Without
.I NAME
the default model is downloaded.
.TP
.B \-\-update\-model
Re-download the default model if its checksum has changed.
.TP
.BI \-\-use\-model " " \fINAME\fR
Set the model in the configuration file permanently.
.TP
.BI \-\-n\-threads " " \fIN\fR
Number of inference threads. 0 means all physical cores. Defaults to the
.B model.n_threads
configuration value, 0 out of the box. Values above the physical core count
reduce performance.
.TP
.BI \-\-n\-gpu\-layers " " \fIN\fR
Layers to offload to the GPU. 0 disables offload. Useful values are the total
layer count or higher.
.TP
.BI \-\-context\-size " " \fIN\fR
Prompt context window in tokens. Range 512 to 32768. Defaults to the
.B model.context_size
configuration value, 4096 out of the box. Below 2048, context and accuracy
degrade noticeably.
.TP
.BI \-\-temperature " " \fIF\fR
Sampling temperature, 0.0 to 2.0. Defaults to the
.B model.temperature
configuration value, 0.2 out of the box. Use 0.0 for deterministic output.
.SS Shell integration
.TP
.B \-\-init
Install the history hook for the detected shell. Idempotent. Modified shell
configuration is delimited by
.B "# >>> gcode init >>>"
and
.BR "# <<< gcode init <<<" .
.TP
.B \-\-init \-\-check
Report whether the hook is installed and which version, without modifying
anything.
.TP
.B \-\-init \-\-remove
Remove the hook, deleting exactly the delimited block and nothing else.
.TP
.BI \-\-generate\-completions " " \fISHELL\fR
Write shell completions for
.BR bash ", " zsh ", or " fish
to standard output.
.SS Diagnostics
.TP
.B \-\-info
Report the inference backend, thread count, GPU layers, and model details.
.TP
.B \-\-bench
Run the standard benchmark and report p50 and p95 latency, tokens per second,
and peak memory.
.TP
.BI \-\-log\-level " " \fILEVEL\fR
One of
.BR error ", " warn ", " info ", " debug ", or " trace .
Default
.BR info .
.TP
.BI \-\-log\-file " " \fIPATH\fR
Additionally write logs to a file.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable ANSI colour. Colour is disabled automatically when standard output is
not a terminal.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit a single JSON object and nothing else. No prompts, no colour. Intended for
scripting.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version, commit hash, and build date.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage information.
.SS Not yet implemented
Not every option below is implemented yet, and the ones that are not are listed
at the end of this section. They are documented because the interface is settled
and the man page is meant to be written once. Passing an unimplemented option
today is an error, not a silent no-op.
.TP
.BR \-\-edit ", " \-\-log\-level ", " \-\-log\-file ", " \-\-verbose ", " \-\-quiet ", " \-\-doctor ", " \-\-check ", " \-\-info ", " \-\-bench ", " \-\-strip\-components ", " \-\-generate\-completions
Diagnostics, editing, and completion generation.
.TP
.BR \-\-list\-models ", " \-\-download\-model ", " \-\-update\-model ", " \-\-use\-model ", " \-\-remove
Model registry management.
.TP
.BR \-\-init ", " \-\-remove ", " \-\-uninstall
Shell hook installation.
.SH INTERACTIVE PROMPT
When confirmation is required, the following keys are accepted:
.TP
.B y
Execute the command.
.TP
.B n
Cancel. Nothing runs. Default at every risk level.
.TP
.B e
Edit the command in
.BR $EDITOR ,
then re-classify and confirm again.
.TP
.B c
Copy the command to the clipboard without executing it.
.TP
.B ?
Explain why the assigned risk level was chosen.
.TP
.B r
Refine the natural language request and generate again.
.PP
.B Ctrl+C
cancels the invocation.
.SH RISK LEVELS
.TP
.B SAFE
Read-only with no side effects.
.TP
.B LOW
Read-only, or a trivial reversible write.
.TP
.B MEDIUM
Broad filesystem traversal, package installation, service restart, or network
fetch.
.TP
.B HIGH
Data deletion, broad permission changes, piping a network download into a shell,
firewall modification, or system power state change.
.TP
.B CRITICAL
Destruction of a filesystem, home directory, or raw block device; fork bombs.
Refused unconditionally. No flag, configuration key, or environment variable
enables execution of a
.B CRITICAL
command.
.PP
Compound commands are split on
.BR ; ", " && ", " || ", and " |
and every segment is classified independently. The overall level is the highest
of any segment.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.gcode/history.jsonl
Append-only command history, one JSON object per line, mode 0600. Rotated at
10 MB, keeping the newest 5 MB as
.I history.jsonl.1
.TP
.I ~/.config/gcode/config.toml
User configuration. Every field is optional, and a missing file is not an
error. An unknown key is refused rather than ignored, so a misspelled setting
is reported instead of silently doing nothing. Override the location with
.B GCODE_CONFIG .
See
.BR gcode (1)
"CONFIGURATION" below for the fields and their defaults.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/gcode/models/
Model cache on Linux.
.TP
.I ~/Library/Application Support/gcode/models/
Model cache on macOS.
.TP
.I /usr/share/gcode/models/
System-wide model directory, used by distribution packages.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The file
.I ~/.config/gcode/config.toml
is TOML. Every field is optional and every setting has a default, so an empty
file is valid.
.PP
Values are merged in one order, lowest priority first: built-in default,
configuration file, environment variable, command-line flag. The defaults live
in the configuration layer, so a flag never carries a hidden default that would
outrank the file.
.PP
An out-of-range value is refused, and so is one from the file. The file never
passes through the argument parser, so it needs checking of its own. The error
names the file, the line, and the field.
.PP
.B safety.always_confirm
may be
.BR SAFE ,
.BR LOW ,
.BR MEDIUM ,
or
.BR HIGH .
It may not be
.BR CRITICAL :
a critical command is never run, so that threshold could never be reached by
anything that prompts, and accepting it would promise more than the tool
delivers.
.PP
.B shell.redact_env
adds to the built-in redaction patterns and can never remove them. Redaction is
a guarantee the tool makes, not a preference the user sets. By contrast
.B safety.blocklist
is replaced when set, because it is a list of commands the user would rather not
see. The blocklist is a convenience and not a safety control: the classifier
decides what is refused to run, and it does not read this list.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GCODE_MODEL
Override the model path. Takes precedence over every other setting.
.TP
.B GCODE_MODEL_MIRROR
Alternate download URL tried after the registry URL fails.
.TP
.B GCODE_CONFIG
Path to an alternative configuration file.
.TP
.B GCODE_NO_HISTORY
If set, do not read or write shell history.
.TP
.B GCODE_NO_INIT
If set, the installer does not modify shell configuration.
.TP
.B GCODE_NO_MODEL
If set, the installer does not download a model.
.TP
.B GCODE_INSTALL_DIR
Directory the installer writes the binary to.
.TP
.B GCODE_HISTORY_FILE
Path to the history file.
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Standard
.B tracing
filter, honoured by
.B \-\-verbose
and
.BR \-\-log\-level .
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Generate a command and review it without executing:
.B gcode \-c "list all files larger than 1GB" \-\-dry\-run
.TP
Repair the last failed command:
.B gcode \-\-fix
.TP
Complete a partial command:
.B gcode \-\-complete "find /var/log \-type f \-name"
.TP
Explain a command without running it:
.B gcode \-\-explain "tar \-xzf backup.tgz \-C /srv \-\-strip\-components=1"
.TP
Scripted use with no colour and no prompts:
.B gcode \-\-json \-n \-c "count files by extension"
.TP
Check the installation:
.B gcode doctor
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, or the user cancelled.
.TP
.B 1
Runtime failure, such as a missing model or an inference error.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command line usage.
.TP
.B 3
The generated command was classified
.B CRITICAL
and was refused.
.SH SECURITY
gcode performs no telemetry, no analytics, and no crash reporting. The only
network request it ever makes is downloading a model file, once, and only when
asked. Model files are verified against a SHA256 checksum pinned in the signed
source repository; a mismatch causes the file to be deleted and the load to be
refused.
.PP
Before the prompt is assembled, environment-derived strings and command output
tails are redacted to remove values matching
.BR *_TOKEN ", " *_SECRET ", " *_KEY ", " *_PASSWORD ", " AWS_* ", "
.BR GITHUB_TOKEN ,
.B Authorization
headers, bearer tokens, PEM private key blocks, and long high-entropy runs.
Redaction is a mitigation, not a guarantee; a secret in an unrecognised format
may pass through. Command output is truncated to the last 2 kilobytes and at
most 15 entries are used by default.
.PP
Decoding is constrained by a shell grammar, so the model cannot emit a token
sequence that is not valid shell. This bounds, but does not eliminate, the
effect of a hostile working directory, filename, or history entry on the
generated command. Risk classification is independent of the model and
re-derived from the emitted text, including after editing.
